> I am once again in doubt what weapon I should use with my ranger.

I've rethought my ranger skill slot write-up but it ends up not
applying to this specific situation as much.

Rangers start with dagger and bow so #enhancing each to
Expert costs 5.  Both should eventually be Expert.
29 - 10 = 19 slots remaining for other uses.

Rangers can #enhance 3 spell schools to ultimately spend
6 slots.  19 - 6 = 13 slots remaining.

Rangers start restricted but I'm going with the LotR model
to figure they will spend a slot each on broadsword and long
sword having received both as gifts even though that's not
the most likely situation.  Chaotic will #name both Sting
and Orcrist early on hoping to end up with Stormy at
crowning or 50-50 as the first gift.  Neutral will get Vorpy
at crowning.  13 - 2 = 11 slots remaining.

Pick axe to basic because I always seem to bash enough
monsters with it.  11 - 1 = 10 slots remaining.

Polearm to skilled because they can and it's fun.  11 - 3 =
7 slots remaining.

Even #enhancing either dart or crossbow to Expert costs
6 but leaves 1 unassigned.  7 - 6 = 1 slot remaining.

Rangers are not limited much by skill slots if they are
willing to foocubus dance to max.

Spend that last slot on anything else for fun.  Maybe riding
to Basic?  Or javelin to be wasteful.  Or whatever random
artifact arrived while wanting other ones.

Having figured out the final spending, when to advance what
is a very open question.

Early on dagger to Expert nearly to the exclusion of other
classes works.  Given an co-aligned mine town altar maybe
long sword or broadsword to Basic by the time both the
mines and Sokoban are done.  Or maybe either darts to
Basic or bow to Skilled.  And eventually move dart to Expert
at no particular phase of the game.

I tend to be around XP=10 when I face Medusa.  5 for
dagger, 1 for a gift sword, 1 for pickaxe, 2 for bow to
Skilled works.  Maybe darts instead of pickaxe.

After Medusa preparing for the Quest I like to play with a
polearm enough to be able to handle both Castles with
a spetum.  Face enough trolls and getting a spetum and
several space polearms is automatic.  Whether anyone but
me will want to spend 3 on polearms to Skilled, I don't know.
Maybe more likely is using a bow from a centaur and
arrows from traps to move bow up in preparation for the
Quest.

Somewhere along here another artifact gift could arrive
and get enhanced to Basic.

That's weapons, so what about spells?  Healing, divination,
escape with invisibility as the ranger's special spell.  If
jumping arrives it's my favorite escape spell to exercise
until escape school is maxed out.  I would do that almost
any time after dagger is Expert.  Other spell schools I would
probably wait until after the Castle to exercise them and
enhance them so I would leave them for last.



